---
const capabilities = [
  'Morning briefings sent to your phone before you open any app (email, calendar, priorities)',
  'Workflows automated across WhatsApp, Telegram, Discord, and Slack',
  'Web research, competitor monitoring, and weekly digests',
  'Meeting audio transcribed, action items pulled out, tasks created in Notion',
  'Custom automations built for how your business actually runs',
  'Memory that carries across sessions, so it knows your context',
];
---

<section id="what" class="section-pad border-t border-white/5">
  <div class="container-md">
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-16 items-start">
      <!-- Left: text -->
      <div>
        <p class="text-accent text-sm font-medium tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">The Platform</p>
        <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-6">What is OpenClaw?</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
          OpenClaw is an open-source AI agent you run on your own machine. It connects to
          WhatsApp, Telegram, or Discord, and does things on your behalf: reading email,
          managing tasks, running searches, scheduling automations.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Most people try ChatGPT, find it useful for drafting things, and leave it there.
          OpenClaw works differently. You set it up once, configure what you want it to watch,
          and it runs in the background handling things without being asked.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm">
          Your data stays on your machine. No vendor cloud. No subscription to OpenClaw itself.
          Just an agent that works for you.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Right: capability list -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        {capabilities.map((cap) => (
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 rounded-lg bg-surface2 border border-white/5">
            <span class="text-accent mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0">→</span>
            <span class="text-neutral-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">{cap}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
